.Sh CONNECTING
Every subcommand that talks to Creature Server takes the same connection options:
.Fl -host ,
.Fl -port
(443 by default, over TLS),
.Fl -insecure
for a plain-HTTP server, and
.Fl -proxy-host
with
.Fl -proxy-api-key
to go through the proxy. The built-in host is a development name; pass the server you mean.
A key given on the command line is visible to every user in
.Xr ps 1 .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev OTEL_*
OpenTelemetry export (OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS,
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL). Without them the command logs to the console only.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Nm
reads no configuration file. The package also ships two relays for the host that bridges the
animatronic network; both are installed disabled.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/creature-sacn-relay.service
Runs
.Ic creature-cli network sacn-listen ,
relaying sACN (E1.31) to TCP viewers on port 1963.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/creature-audio-relay.service
Runs
.Ic creature-cli network rtp-listen ,
relaying live RTP audio to TCP viewers on port 1964.
.It Pa /etc/default/creature-relay
Settings both relays share:
.Ev RELAY_INTERFACE ,
the interface wired to the animatronic network, and
.Ev RELAY_SACN_EXTRA_ARGS ,
.Ev RELAY_AUDIO_EXTRA_ARGS
for extra options. Enable a relay with
.Dl systemctl enable --now creature-sacn-relay
.It Pa /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/creature-cli
Completion for bash; zsh and fish completions are installed alongside.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
List the creatures on a server:
.Dl creature-cli creatures list --host server.example.com
Help for any subcommand:
.Dl creature-cli help animations
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr creature-mqtt 8 ,
.Xr creature-world 8
